{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Find mortgage loan officers"},"description":"Use this when someone wants a US mortgage loan officer (or mortgage broker or lender contact) for a specific situation and place: for example an FHA, VA, USDA, jumbo, DSCR or ITIN loan, a first-time buyer, a self-employed borrower who needs a bank statement loan, a non-warrantable condo or a duplex, or a Spanish-speaking loan officer near a city, ZIP, region or state. Searches LenDb, an independent, lender-neutral database of US loan officers (coverage is partial), and returns a ranked list. Each result has the person's name, NMLS ID, lender, office location, distance_mi, reasons[], license_check for the property state (confirmed, lender_reported or federal_registration), match_status (exact, or partial with unconfirmed_specialties) and a canonical_url profile link. A city or ZIP keeps offices within 25 miles, widened to 50 or 100 when few are found (search.note); a state alone ranks statewide. Words like 'broker' or 'credit union' rank that kind of lender first. People with no license evidence for the state are listed separately in not_yet_verified. Also returns ambiguous_location when a city name fits several places, unassessed_requirements for parts of the situation LenDb cannot check, and citation_guidance. If situation is just a loan officer's name (the name on their lender page or the name a state regulator licenses, e.g. 'Nicholas Bucca' for Nic Bucca), it returns that profile in profile_match. Phone numbers and email addresses are never returned.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"debug":{"description":"Also return how the query was parsed (debug.parsed, debug.filters). Default false.","type":"boolean"},"fha_approved":{"description":"Only loan officers whose current lender is FHA-approved per HUD's FHA Single Family Portfolio Snapshot data (the lender, not the person). Default false. Without it, an FHA search still ranks HUD-approved lenders' people first when all else is equal.","type":"boolean"},"language":{"description":"Language the borrower wants to be served in. Accepts an ISO 639-1 code ('es'), a BCP 47 tag ('es-MX', 'zh-TW'), an ISO 639-2/3 code ('spa'), an English name ('Spanish') or a native name ('espa\u00f1ol', '\u4e2d\u6587', '\ud55c\uad6d\uc5b4', 'ti\u1ebfng Vi\u1ec7t'). A hard filter: every result speaks it. An unsupported language returns an error listing the supported codes (see list_specialties).","maxLength":60,"type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"Max results, default 10.","maximum":25,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"location":{"description":"Where the property is: 'City, ST', a city, a 5-digit ZIP, a region ('Bay Area'), or a US state.","maxLength":200,"minLength":2,"type":"string"},"situation":{"description":"The borrower's situation in plain words: property type, loan program, income type, credit, language, kind of lender. Example: 'duplex, self-employed, bank statement loan'.","maxLength":500,"minLength":2,"type":"string"}},"required":["situation","location"],"type":"object"},"name":"find_loan_officers","outputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":{},"properties":{"all_terms_understood":{"type":"boolean"},"ambiguous_location":{"additionalProperties":{},"properties":{"note":{"type":"string"},"options":{"items":{"additionalProperties":{},"properties":{"label":{"type":"string"},"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["label","query"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"term":{"type":"string"}},"required":["term","note","options"],"type":"object"},"canonical_url":{"description":"The same search on the LenDb API.","type":"string"},"citation_guidance":{"type":"string"},"count":{"type":"number"},"debug":{"additionalProperties":{},"description":"Only when the call set debug: true.","properties":{"filters":{},"parsed":{}},"required":["parsed","filt